f the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n2927,SPERMATOZOA,Spermatozoa are male reproductive cells that are tested for survival under various experimental conditions.,5\r\n2924,SODIUM CITRATE,\"**Sodium Citrate: Comprehensive Summary**\n\n**Definition and Purpose**  \nSodium citrate is a chemical compound that serves multiple roles in experimental settings, particularly in biological and biochemical research. It is commonly utilized as a buffering agent and anticoagulant, and it has been specifically noted for its application in experiments related to spermatozoa survival. The primary purpose of using sodium citrate in such experiments is to create an optimal environment that enhances the viability and functionality of sperm cells during various experimental procedures.\n\n**Mathematical Formulation or Model Structure**  \nWhile sodium citrate itself does not have a specific mathematical formulation, its effects can be incorporated into experimental models as a design factor. In the context of a factorial design, the concentration of sodium citrate can be treated as an independent variable, influencing the dependent variable, which in this case is spermatozoa survival rate. The general model structure can be represented as:\n\n\\[ Y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 X_1 + \\beta_2 X_2 + ... + \\beta_k X_k + \\epsilon \\]\n\nwhere \\( Y \\) is the response variable (spermatozoa survival), \\( \\beta_0 \\) is the intercept, \\( \\beta_i \\) are the coefficients for each factor \\( X_i \\) (including sodium citrate), and \\( \\epsilon \\) is the error term.\n\n**Design Layout or Structure**  \nIn experiments involving sodium citrate, a factorial design may be employed to assess its impact alongside other factors. The design layout could include varying concentra